ef 1068 #edb/ref 17592186220231 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221939 #edb/ref 1069 "q-330839" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221939 #edb/ref 1071 "For the function\n$G(s) = (1)/(s(s - 3)), s > 3$\nfind the inverse Laplace transform of $G(s)$, given that\n$L{e^{at}} = \\frac{1}{s - a}, s > a$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221939 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "20b122a8-4745-5793-8bbf-3ef6f005a663" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222352 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186222353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222352 #edb/ref 1061 599887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222352 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e6f15f22-f7c7-5bf4-a482-3a5056a94c4b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222352 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186222478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222353 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186222354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222353 #edb/ref 1061 599888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222353 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "56307df4-da62-5ba2-8afa-b2b66440392e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222353 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186222525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222354 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186222355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222354 #edb/ref 1061 599889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222354 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a43eec6c-67d4-51d6-8cd3-dbcb10285abe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222354 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186221430 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222355 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186222356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222355 #edb/ref 1061 599893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222355 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "312c0532-dea4-5d89-a008-f3c01af9788f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222355 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186221431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222356 #edb/ref 1061 599897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222356 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1a92f22b-d74e-54dd-8892-21a9e187fa2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222356 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186221432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222478 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose a quantity increases over time at a rate proportional to its current value, such as the balance of a bank account growing with continuous interest. The Laplace transform can be used to analyze how such exponential growth behaves, especially when the function is **integrated over time** to represent total accumulation.\n\nTo illustrate this, we’ll find the Laplace transform of a function defined as the integral of an exponential function. This shows how *integration in the time domain* corresponds to *division by $s$* in the $s$-domain.\n\nSuppose we are given that \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\{e^{at}\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s-a}, \\qquad s>a.\n$$\n\nLet's find the Laplace transform of\n\n$$\ng(t) = \\int_{0}^{t} e^{\\tau/2}\\,\\mathrm{d}\\tau,\n\\qquad s > \\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe apply the **Integration in Time Property**: if $\\mathcal{L}\\{f(t)\\} = F(s)$, then\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{\\int_{0}^{t} f(\\tau)\\,\\mathrm{d}\\tau \\right\\} = \\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(t)=e^{t/2}$. Thus, for $s>\\dfrac{1}{2},$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =L\\{f(t)\\} \\\\  & =L\\{{e}^{t/2}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(s-\\frac{1}{2})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the integral identity above, we have for $s>\\dfrac{1}{2},$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{g(t)\\} & =L\\,\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{τ/2}\\,dτ\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s\\,(s-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s(2s-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222478 #edb/ref 1065 14359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222478 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ee57f084-2127-562e-bf7b-91641db97ba1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222478 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222525 #edb/ref 1064 "Assume that\n\n- $f(t)$ is *piecewise continuous* on $[0,\\infty)$, and\n\n- $f(t)$ is of exponential order $a$.\n\nThen the Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=\\mathcal L\\{f(t)\\}\n$$\n\nexists for all $s>a$, and we have the **Integration Property**:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal L\\!\\left\\{\\int_0^t f(\\tau)\\,\\textrm{d}\\tau\\right\\}\n= \\frac{F(s)}{s},\n\\qquad s>a.\n$$\n\nThis result shows that *integrating a function with respect to time* corresponds to *dividing its Laplace transform by $s$*.  \n\nThis result allows us to handle accumulated quantities without re-integrating from scratch.\n\nNext, we will apply this property to a concrete example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222525 #edb/ref 1065 14729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222525 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "05dac555-11de-5a37-a12e-e9c6ad069388" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222525 #edb/ref 1067 "The General Result" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302571 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302571 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302571 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "11988bb4-bd76-5da0-89ba-38a30472093a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302824 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{s-5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302824 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302824 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3b30fb93-d4f5-57ff-89d5-4ae27e848f3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302827 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{t}^{6}}{30}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302827 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302827 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3b6e7e94-7dde-537c-98cb-20b59c24b1fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302897 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{5}(1-{e}^{5t})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302897 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302897 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "45bc93fe-5bb2-55dd-8c94-74f48290abdc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303013 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{24}{{t}^{5}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303013 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303013 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5b39dec8-6f4d-5a1c-8367-b4a6120b8574" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303100 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{t}-1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303100 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303100 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "69b71edb-5681-5b89-9393-9ba3e46b6fbd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303108 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303108 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303108 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6aa8899d-beae-5941-a3d4-82e94a1d2266" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303176 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{5t}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303176 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303176 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "75e53d4a-6a6b-5a91-815b-dc87331bce6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303204 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{5t}-1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303204 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303204 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7906a1bc-f57e-5117-b624-76a26363e3f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303890 #edb/ref 1080 "{t}^{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303890 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303890 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e6893c52-98ee-5b15-a3f0-a746742b6299" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304367 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186302824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304367 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186302897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304367 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304367 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304367 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304367 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304367 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304367 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186303204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304367 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6c0df3ef-2be2-59de-94c6-d27577149ad2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186302571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186302827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304476 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304476 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304476 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186303108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304476 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "95522057-6f76-5a8c-85b6-0d8377b32c14" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304857 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304857 #edb/ref 1069 "q-330843" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304857 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304857 #edb/ref 1071 "For the function\n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{24}{{s}^{6}},\\,s>0\n$$\n\nfind the inverse Laplace transform of $G(s),$ given that\n$L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304857 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c43f625b-d110-5aef-9243-2a1cae536c09" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304857 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that we can write $G(s)$ as \n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{24}{{s}^{6}}=\\frac{F(s)}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $F(s)=\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}.$\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.\n$$\n\nThus, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{F(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4!}{{s}^{4+1}}} \\\\  & ={t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nUsing the property above in reverse, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{G(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{F(s)}{s}} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}{τ}^{4}\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304859 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304367 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304859 #edb/ref 1069 "q-330849" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304859 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304859 #edb/ref 1071 "For the function\n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s(s-5)},\\,s>5\n$$\n\nfind the inverse Laplace transform of $G(s),$ given that\n$L{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a},\\text{ }s>a.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304859 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8064a487-d480-5cc5-97a5-d474531a9775" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304859 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that we can write $G(s)$ as \n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s(s-5)}=\\frac{F(s)}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $F(s)=\\frac{1}{s-5}.$\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\nL{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a}.\n$$\n\nThus, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{F(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-5}} \\\\  & ={e}^{5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nUsing the property above in reverse, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{G(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{F(s)}{s}} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{5τ}\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5τ}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{5t}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370100 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186370101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370100 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186370106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370100 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186370111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370100 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186370114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370100 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186370119 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370100 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186370124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370100 #edb/ref 1069 "q-331076" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370100 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370100 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we wish to find $L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ}$ given $L{f(t)}=F(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.Let $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ={{field-1}}\\,{|}_{0}^{t}=A(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ}=L{A(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & ⇒ & du={A}^{′}(t)\\text{ }dt \\\\ dv={{field-3}} & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & =A(t)(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({{field-4}}){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=$ {{field-5}}, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt=\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-6}}\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370100 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c7ba6935-6849-517e-9bd9-9735ae2d6fb9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370100 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ & =A(τ)\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =A(t)-A(0) \\\\  & =A(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ} & =L{A(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & \\,⇒\\, & du={A}^{′}(t)\\,dt \\\\ dv={e}^{-st}\\,dt & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & =A(t)(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A(0)=0$ and $\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ we have $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=0$ and\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt=\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot F(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370101 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370101 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370101 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370104 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370101 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370101 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370101 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370101 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186370104 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370101 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "10807e40-8603-55ae-8902-22cd7325d252" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370102 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{t}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370102 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370102 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "94356250-04c6-5d39-ba5d-7e4b6a1c3617" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370103 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{st}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370103 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370103 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6af64c5a-daef-5659-9f22-bad50ed6662a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370104 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{-st}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759